    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This charming family or holiday home is set on approximately 0.59 acres in a peaceful countryside setting on the outskirts of Kilmore, just 20 km from Wexford. The property enjoys an excellent coastal location and is practically a stone’s throw from the beautiful beaches at Ballyhealy Beach & Seaview Beach. The picturesque seaside village of Kilmore Quay is also nearby. Scenic walking routes can be enjoyed at Tacumshane Lake & Our Lady’s Island Lake, both located only a short distance away. All essential amenities including shops, schools, churches, supermarkets, pharmacy, post office & many popular restaurants are conveniently available in the nearby villages of Kilmore, Bridgetown and Kilmore Quay. For travel and commuting, Rosslare Europort is approximately 20 km away, offering ferry connections to the UK and Europe. The property also has easy access to the N25 road (Ireland) and M11 motorway (Ireland), providing convenient connections to Dublin and Cork. The accommodation includes an entrance porch, living room, kitchen/diner, inner hallway, bathroom and utility room on the ground fl\u001door. Upstairs there are three double bedrooms including a master bedroom with en suite, along with a Jack and Jill shower room serving the remaining two bedrooms. Outside, the property benefits from gardens to the side and rear with spacious parking available. A further highlight is the ruins of a historic stone-built cottage located on the site. The remains present a rare opportunity to create a unique residence and place your own stamp on a piece of history, with previous planning permission granted for conversion.\r\nThis is a truly beautiful countryside and seaside location offering an ideal opportunity for those seeking a peaceful home in one of South Wexford’s most scenic areas."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Property Accommodation\r\nEntrance Hallway – (1.9mx 1.8m), Tile flooring.\r\nLiving Room – (4.6m x 3.7m), Laminate timber flooring, stove.\r\nInner Hallway – (5.2m x 1m), Tile flooring, Hotpress, understairs storage.\r\nKitchen/ Diner – (4.6m x 3.5m), Tile flooring, cabinets at waist and eye level. rear garden, HP with storage.\r\nUtility Room – (2.5m x 2.5m ), Tile flooring, cabinets at waist and eye level, plumbed for washing machine.\r\nBathroom –  (2.7m x 2.9m), Tile flooring, WC, WHB.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nLanding  – (5.4m x 1.5m)\r\nBedroom No. 1 – (4.5m x 3.5m), Laminate timber flooring.\r\nEn Suite – (1.7m x 1.7m), Tile flooring, WC, WHB, shower.\r\nBedroom No. 2  – (4.4m x 3.7m), Laminate timber flooring, access to shower room.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (3m x 2.7m), Laminate timber flooring, access to shower room.\r\nShower Room -(2m x 1.3m), Tile flooring, WC, WHB, enclosed shower.\r\n\r\nOutside: Ample parking, grass surrounding.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: D1 Ber No: 119148872 Performance indicator: 249.45 kWh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
